# Line endings are normalised to LF inside the repository, while the working
# tree keeps whatever the platform uses. Without this, files written with CRLF
# on Windows compare byte-for-byte against LF blobs and every single line reads
# as modified — a two-line test edit showed up as a 1,521-line diff.
#
# `text=auto` lets Git decide which files are text and leaves anything binary
# alone, so nothing needs listing by hand.
* text=auto
